# Shopify Theme — Auto Push After Changes

This workspace is the **POSTERLEAGUE** Shopify theme. After making **any** change to theme files (liquid, css, js, json, assets, snippets, sections, etc.), **always push to the live theme** before ending the turn — do not wait for the user to ask.

## Store & theme

| Key | Value |
|-----|-------|
| Store | `posterleague-cz54479w.myshopify.com` |
| Theme ID | `153070796961` |
| Local folder | `E:\posterleague-theme` |

## Push command

**Always ignore template JSON and settings_data** so Theme Editor uploads (videos, images, section blocks) are NOT wiped on push:

```powershell
cd E:\posterleague-theme
shopify theme push --store posterleague-cz54479w.myshopify.com --theme 153070796961 --allow-live --ignore "templates/*.json" --ignore "config/settings_data.json"
```

## Why ignore those files?

- `templates/*.json` — homepage hero videos, section blocks, and page layout from Theme Editor live here. Pushing local copies **deletes** uploaded videos.
- `config/settings_data.json` — global theme settings (floating video, colors toggled in admin) live here.

Only push those files when **intentionally** syncing layout defaults from code (and warn the user first).

## When to push

- After editing sections, snippets, layout, assets, config schema, locales, or CSS/JS
- After creating or deleting theme files
- Even for small CSS/JS tweaks — push immediately

## When NOT to push

- Question-only or review-only tasks with no file edits
- Non-theme files only (e.g. docs outside the theme, cursor rules)

## On push failure

- Report the error clearly
- Do not claim changes are live until push succeeds
- Retry once if it looks like a transient network/auth issue
